WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.675 --> 00:00:10.468
The oldest cultures

00:00:11.344 --> 00:00:13.221
are not human.

00:00:16.266 --> 00:00:18.393
They're from the ocean.

00:00:19.102 --> 00:00:20.895
40 million years ago

00:00:20.895 --> 00:00:22.647
before we walked upright, 

00:00:23.481 --> 00:00:24.691
before we sparked fire - 

00:00:26.109 --> 00:00:27.360
Whales evolved 

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:28.820
to build relationships

00:00:29.362 --> 00:00:30.405
in the dark.

00:00:33.199 --> 00:00:35.744
I'm trying to start
a conversation -

00:00:36.119 --> 00:00:38.997
- is the most basic way
you can say it.

00:00:41.207 --> 00:00:43.460
I'm trying to put a speaker
in the ocean

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:45.920
and talk to a whale and
hope it talks back.

00:00:45.962 --> 00:00:46.796
Starting playback.

00:00:48.256 --> 00:00:50.383
If this work is successful

00:00:50.383 --> 00:00:52.260
it would be the first
experiment

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:53.720
where we have engaged
in a dialogue

00:00:53.928 --> 00:00:54.929
with a humpback whale.

00:00:58.767 --> 00:01:00.643
People have been studying
humpback songs

00:01:00.643 --> 00:01:02.187
for 40 or 50 years.

00:01:04.272 --> 00:01:05.148
And still

00:01:05.148 --> 00:01:07.025
no one really knows

00:01:07.317 --> 00:01:08.651
why they sing.

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:13.573
Something different

00:01:13.782 --> 00:01:15.200
is happening here.

00:01:19.078 --> 00:01:22.499
The study has a high
probability of failure.

00:01:24.042 --> 00:01:25.293
We have only a month

00:01:25.293 --> 00:01:27.212
to survey at least 30 whales.

00:01:29.506 --> 00:01:31.674
It is so hard to interpret
the language

00:01:31.674 --> 00:01:33.301
of the natural world.

00:01:35.011 --> 00:01:36.095
To listen

00:01:36.095 --> 00:01:37.472
and to understand

00:01:39.349 --> 00:01:40.183
what it's saying

00:01:40.809 --> 00:01:41.893
to itself.

00:01:42.852 --> 00:01:44.771
That is of the same proportion

00:01:44.771 --> 00:01:47.690
as pointing all of our
satellites skyward 

00:01:47.690 --> 00:01:49.943
and listening for a sign
from outer space.

00:01:50.652 --> 00:01:51.319
Pretty cool.

00:01:51.528 --> 00:01:52.445
That's pretty cool.

00:01:52.904 --> 00:01:54.823
They're talking back to you.

00:02:06.251 --> 00:02:07.794
Studying whale culture

00:02:09.128 --> 00:02:10.922
might be more about
glimpsing

00:02:10.922 --> 00:02:12.173
something of ourselves.

00:02:14.509 --> 00:02:16.511
How we can connect differently

00:02:17.679 --> 00:02:19.639
a million years from now.

